# Reggie James: full profile

Website: {{ site.url }}
Positioning: The right decisions change everything. I help tech leaders make the ones that grow their business.
Who he works with: founders, CEOs and leadership teams of B2B technology companies between value proposition and exit, and the VC, private equity and private investors who back them.
Location: Guildford, Surrey, and London, United Kingdom.

## What clients get

### Go-to-market strategy
Ideal customer and segment priorities; positioning and a proposition buyers understand; pricing and packaging review; the right sales motion and channels; a growth accelerator programme built around where the company is today.

### Marketing that builds pipeline
Messaging senior buyers respond to; a demand and pipeline model tied to revenue targets; content, channel and partner plan; visibility in AI search and answer engines; reporting the board can trust.

### Execution and commercial leadership
Hands-on leadership of sales and marketing; sales, marketing and product aligned to one plan; the right commercial team and structure; agencies and partners selected and held to account; monthly or fractional executive involvement.

### For investors: commercial due diligence and portfolio growth
Pre-deal commercial and go-to-market assessment; proposition, market and competitor review; a portfolio accelerator for companies behind plan; go-to-market reviews across the portfolio; ongoing support for portfolio leadership teams.

### How engagements start
A discovery call, then a go-to-market review scoped on that call, then delivery on a monthly or fractional basis. Digital Clarity provides a delivery team when a programme needs one.

## Track record
- Founded Digital Clarity in 2002; grew it to 25 to 30 people and more than 200 clients, including Adobe, Xerox and Bentley Systems.
- Built DC Storm, a marketing measurement platform used by around 48% of major media planning and buying agencies, acquired by Rakuten.
- Led commercial operations for an internet business in Singapore that listed on SIMEX and was acquired.
- COO, Senior Vice President and Executive Director of DBMM Group Inc. (OTC: DBMM) since 2011.
- Earlier: AltaVista global sales (HP, Compaq); technology publishing at VNU and Ziff Davis.
- Client results: software ARR from $8m to $23m in three years; 88% EMEA revenue growth in 12 months with cost per acquisition down 37.6%; 30% more qualified demo requests year on year.

